+### Proposed, awaiting the steward: which skill writes guards
+
+*Raised 2026-10-07 by an entropy assessment. Not decided. `INTENT.md` stays as it is until the steward records a decision here.*
+
+**Context**: Guard writing is described in three ways. `INTENT.md` "The guard lifecycle" gives the generator role to `skills/entropy-assessment/` and `skills/docs-first-planning-assessment/`. `docs-first-planning-assessment` Phase 2 writes guards. `skills/session-coherence-skill-generator/` (metadata dated 2026-05-10) also writes them, to `skills/session-coherence-guard/SKILL.md`, and `README.md` and `AGENTS.md` list it as generating guards. No entry here adds that skill or gives it the role; "Session-coherence generation should bootstrap young repos before generating guards" assumes it exists. Neither assessment skill routes to it, and its guard requirements do not include the integration instructions that "Guards need closed-loop integration, not just checklist files" requires of generators.
+**Proposal**: One skill writes guards: `session-coherence-skill-generator`. `docs-first-planning-assessment` keeps its analysis and supplies its docs-first checks to the generator, and the generator hands to `guards-integrator`. Reasons: it is the only skill with a written guard contract; it covers every repo shape, young repos included; and "Consolidate domain generators into single skill with domain appendices" already rejected keeping duplicated generation scaffolding in parallel.
+**Impact if accepted**: `INTENT.md` "The guard lifecycle", `README.md`, `skills/guards-integrator/SKILL.md` "When to Run" and `docs-first-planning-assessment` Phase 2 change to match.
+
+---
+
+### Proposed, awaiting the steward: how the intent changes
+
+*Raised 2026-10-07 by an entropy assessment. Not decided. `INTENT.md` and `AGENTS.md` stay as they are until the steward records a decision here.*
+
+**Context**: `INTENT.md`'s header and closing line invite anyone, agents included, to refine it directly with a dated note. `AGENTS.md` "Consult INTENT.md for significant decisions" says to update `INTENT.md` when a decision refines or challenges the intent, and the local guard's check 3 says the same. So the session whose work drifted from the intent can also rewrite the intent, and the next check then finds no drift. `INTENT.md` says intent entropy "decays slowly but is catastrophic to recover". Nothing records who may change the intent.
+**Proposal**: A contributor records a proposed intent change here, marked as awaiting the steward. `INTENT.md` changes only after the steward's recorded decision, keeping its dated-note convention for that edit.
+**Impact if accepted**: The header and closing line of `INTENT.md` and the last bullet of `AGENTS.md` "Working Practices" change to match. The local guard drafted on 2026-10-07, not yet installed, already follows this rule.
+
